# Live Hosting a Collaborative Session

You can sync your window scrolling with your collaborators, as if you&#39;re live streaming a collaborative note. This is helpful when you&#39;re in a meeting and you want others to see what you&#39;re seeing.

Click on the top right **&lt;i class=&#34;fa fa-users&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt; ? ONLINE** button, and you can assign the host who will share the view he/she sees.

In the below gif demo, User B is hosting the note so User A can see where she is referring to.

![start hosting a note](https://hackmd.io/_uploads/rJG7ktKwR.gif)

:::info
:bulb: **Hint**: Only people with Admin permission on the note (note owner and invited admins) have the privilege to assign host. It is not unexpected if people fight for hosting. :grin:
:::

[Learn more about invited admins.](/c/tutorials/%2Fs%2Finvite)

# Un-follow and Resume Following
When someone else is hosting the note but you want to check out different section of the note, you can unfollow the host from the same dropdown menu.

![unfollow host](https://hackmd.io/_uploads/SkGjXKtP0.gif)

And when you are ready to resume following, click ++follow++ again and you would jump right to the host&#39;s current focus.

![image](https://hackmd.io/_uploads/HJ_O0_KPR.png =300x)

